    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0727" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/5–654:Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States
                            Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-06T11:00:00+01:00">May 6, 1954—11 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 111. Repeated information Saigon 35,
                    Paris 204, London 124. Reference Saigon telegram 2202 repeated Geneva 44, Paris
                        752.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d438-f1"/> I concur with Saigon that the Secretary
                    might at his next press conference, in reply to a question regarding possible
                    partition of Vietnam, say that the United States advocates a solution firmly
                    based upon the independence, unity and the territorial and political integrity
                    of Vietnam.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
